## Task: Create a standard Python project structure

- [ ] Initialize a new project named `teleforward`
- [ ] Set up a virtual environment using `venv`
- [ ] Create a `Makefile` with the following commands:
  - [ ] `make install` — install dependencies from `requirements.txt`
  - [ ] `make run` — run the main Python script
- [ ] Create a `src/` directory and place `main.py` inside
- [ ] Add a `README.md` with the following instructions:
  - [ ] How to create and activate the virtual environment
  - [ ] How to install dependencies
  - [ ] How to run the project
- [ ] Add a `.gitignore` file for a typical Python project

## Task: Set up unit testing infrastructure

- [ ] Create a `tests/` directory for test files
- [ ] Add test dependencies to `requirements.txt`:
  - [ ] `pytest` - for running tests
  - [ ] `pytest-cov` - for test coverage
  - [ ] `pytest-mock` - for mocking in tests
- [ ] Create a basic test configuration in `pytest.ini`
- [ ] Add test commands to `Makefile`:
  - [ ] `make test` - run all tests
  - [ ] `make test-cov` - run tests with coverage report
- [ ] Create a sample test file to demonstrate the testing structure